      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | DeSales University Home Position: Assistant Director of Graduate Admission Location: Center Valley, PA Job Id: 276 # of Openings: 1 ASSISTANT DIRECTOR OF GRADUATE ADMISSION OVERVIEW: DeSales University, in Center Valley, PA, is a private, coeducational, four-year liberal arts Salesian, Catholic university, under the leadership of the Oblates of Saint Francis de Sales. Founded in 1965, the 550-acre suburban campus is located 50 miles north of Philadelphia and about 90 miles southwest of New York City. A total enrollment of nearly 3,500 includes undergraduate day and evening students, and graduate students. DeSales has approximately 135 full-time faculty members and offers more than 40 bachelor's degrees, twelve graduate programs, and over 20 certificate programs in a wide range of disciplines; many of these can be completed fully online. In 2024, the University transitioned to a new academic structure featuring a four-college/school model, which includes the Kathleen Waterbury and J.B. Reilly School of Business; a College of Arts, Education, and Humanities with a School of Education and a School of Performing Arts; a College of Sciences; and a College of Healthcare Professions with a designated School of Nursing. For further information, visit www.desales.edu. EOE POSITION SUMMARY: The Assistant Director of Graduate Admission supports the recruitment of prospective students. As an integral member of the Graduate Admission team, this role operates in a highly customer service–oriented environment and contributes to the success of the college’s recruitment efforts. Responsibilities include coordinating recruitment events such as open houses, information sessions, and university visits; maximizing the use of the Slate recruitment platform; managing assigned territories; and achieving admission goals for designated graduate programs. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required from an accredited institution Must demonstrate ability to work within a team-oriented environment, possess strong communication and organizational skills, and experienced in public speaking with the ability to develop engaging presentations. At least 1-3 years’ experience working with adult learners at an academic institution. Proficient computer skills; CRM experience a plus. Self-directed and must demonstrate a keen understanding of effective customer service concepts. Work some evening and weekend hours throughout the year, travel is required. Valid driver’s license with clean driving record. Sensitive to issues of ethnicity, disability, and diversity Dedicated to the mission of a small, catholic, liberal arts institution DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by DeSales University"
