      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | DeSales University Home Position: Technical Services and Instruction Librarian Location: Center Valley, PA Job Id: 275 # of Openings: 1 TECHNICAL SERVICES AND INSTRUCTION LIBRARIAN OVERVIEW: DeSales University, in Center Valley, PA, is a private, coeducational, four-year liberal arts Salesian, Catholic university, under the leadership of the Oblates of Saint Francis de Sales. Founded in 1965, the 550-acre suburban campus is located 50 miles north of Philadelphia and about 90 miles southwest of New York City. A total enrollment of nearly 3,500 includes undergraduate day and evening students, and graduate students. DeSales has approximately 135 full-time faculty members and offers more than 40 bachelor's degrees, twelve graduate programs, and over 20 certificate programs in a wide range of disciplines; many of these can be completed fully online. In 2024, the University transitioned to a new academic structure featuring a four-college/school model, which includes the Kathleen Waterbury and J.B. Reilly School of Business; a College of Arts, Education, and Humanities with a School of Education and a School of Performing Arts; a College of Sciences; and a College of Healthcare Professions with a designated School of Nursing. For further information, visit www.desales.edu. EOE POSITION SUMMARY: Technical Services and Instruction Librarian provides course related library instruction in face-to-face and online courses with a special focus on outreach to our business, performing arts, philosophy and theology students. The librarian creates teaching materials and other resources that enhance the library’s teaching and learning services and collaborates with other instruction librarians on general and virtual research and reference services. This position is part of the Technical Services Team, and the Instruction Team. QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in Library Science required Excellent skills in both verbal and written communication Familiarity with information literacy pedagogy including assessment methods Requires a work schedule of 9am to 5pm Monday through Friday. Some off-hour support will be required throughout the semester supporting 2 weeks of finals, specifically evening and weekends as needed. Sensitive to issues of ethnicity, disability and diversity Dedicated to the mission of a small, Catholic, liberal arts institution DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by DeSales University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d0930d0e990193232e613f0336&id=8a7883aca03fc27d01a063268eee0837&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | DeSales University Home Position: Office Coordinator: Registrar's Office Location: Center Valley, PA Job Id: 277 # of Openings: 1 OFFICE COORDINATOR: REGISTRAR'S OFFICE Overview: DeSales University, in Center Valley, PA, is a private, coeducational, four-year liberal arts Salesian, Catholic university, under the leadership of the Oblates of Saint Francis de Sales. Founded in 1965, the 550-acre suburban campus is located 50 miles north of Philadelphia and about 90 miles southwest of New York City. A total enrollment of nearly 3,500 includes undergraduate day and evening students, and graduate students. DeSales has approximately 135 full-time faculty members and offers more than 40 bachelor's degrees, twelve graduate programs, and over 20 certificate programs in a wide range of disciplines; many of these can be completed fully online. In 2024, the University transitioned to a new academic structure featuring a four-college/school model, which includes the Kathleen Waterbury and J.B. Reilly School of Business; a College of Arts, Education, and Humanities with a School of Education and a School of Performing Arts; a College of Sciences; and a College of Healthcare Professions with a designated School of Nursing. For further information, visit www.desales.edu. Position Summary: The Office Coordinator is responsible for inventory control and the budget.  S/he will also work closely with the Graduate Departments to set up course offerings, maintain enrollment and assure that all grades are entered in a timely basis. This position will deal with students/faculty/staff in a professional and courteous manner. S/he is responsible for the successful administration for the Graduate programs in the Registrar’s Office: ensuring that Graduate course schedules are posted in a timely manner, registration proceeds efficiently each session, and graduation lists are coordinated with Graduate Offices prior to each degree conferral date. The Office Coordinator is responsible for entering transfer credits, change of majors, adding minors, and assisting in the office as needed to meet our goals of providing excellent customer service. Qualifications: Associates degree and/or equivalent experience Experience in a higher educational administrative office Commitment to professional development and teamwork Sensitive to issues of ethnicity, disability and diversity Dedicated to the mission of a small, Catholic, liberal arts institution DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by DeSales University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d0930d0e990193232e613f0336&id=8a78859f9f44356c019f84f87f3408d3&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | DeSales University Home Position: Properties Supervisor Location: Center Valley, PA Job Id: 267 # of Openings: 1 PROPERTIES SUPERVISOR OVERVIEW: DeSales University, in Center Valley, PA, is a private, coeducational, four-year liberal arts Salesian, Catholic university, under the leadership of the Oblates of Saint Francis de Sales. Founded in 1965, the 550-acre suburban campus is located 50 miles north of Philadelphia and about 90 miles southwest of New York City. A total enrollment of nearly 3,500 includes undergraduate day and evening students, and graduate students. DeSales has approximately 135 full-time faculty members and offers more than 40 bachelor's degrees, twelve graduate programs, and over 20 certificate programs in a wide range of disciplines; many of these can be completed fully online. In 2024, the University transitioned to a new academic structure featuring a four-college/school model, which includes the Kathleen Waterbury and J.B. Reilly School of Business; a College of Arts, Education, and Humanities with a School of Education and a School of Performing Arts; a College of Sciences; and a College of Healthcare Professions with a designated School of Nursing. For further information, visit www.desales.edu. EOE POSITION SUMMARY: The Properties Supervisor is responsible for the procurement, budgeting. and building of all properties for the DeSales Act 1 season.  They will also supervise the student props practicum and assist in the facilitation of the scene shop practicum. This position includes mentoring student leaders on student projects. The maintenance and organization of the props storage area as well as the occasional rental of properties to outside organizations. QUALIFICATIONS: Undergraduate degree required; graduate-level degree preferred Excellent organizational, communication, budgetary, and interpersonal skills required. Experience in all aspects of properties construction (stitching, carpentry, upholstery, painting, etc.) required, experience in welding ideal Periodic weekend and weeknight availability required Dedicated to the mission of a small, Catholic, liberal arts institution DeSales University is an EEO employer - M/F/Vets/Disabled Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by DeSales University"
    }
